# Secrets — an Enable Banking private key opens your bank data.
# Once a .pem is in git history, removing it means rewriting history.
*.pem
*.key
.clasp.json
.clasprc.json

# Deployment ids. Not credentials, but the app door is access-MYSELF at a URL
# nobody is meant to have, and this repo is public. .deploy.example.json is the
# committed half. See docs/DEPLOY.md.
.deploy.json

# Data — never commit a transaction history to a public repo.
*.csv
*.xlsx
snapshots/
exports/

# Tooling
node_modules/
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Agent worktrees. Each is a checkout of this same repo, so `git add -A` offers
# them as embedded repositories and `npm test` collects their copy of every
# test file — 3,583 tests over four checkouts, of which 899 are this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# Playwright MCP scratch (snapshots, screenshots) — never part of the repo
.playwright-mcp/

# What a failed `npm run test:e2e` leaves behind: traces, screenshots and the
# HTML report. Every one of them is a recording of the app with this book's
# numbers on the screen, which is the same reason `*.csv` is above.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# The web viewer's build output and local secrets. `.dev.vars` is what
# `wrangler dev` reads, so it holds the OAuth client secret and the key that
# seals every session in the clear — the same reason `*.pem` is at the top of
# this file, arriving by a new door.
web/dist/
web/.wrangler/
web/.dev.vars
# Who the viewer admits: Google account IDs and the addresses beside them.
# People, not configuration, and the repository is public.
web/.accounts.json

# Credentials that arrive as files: a Google OAuth client download (the
# viewer's setup reads one), a service account, a PKCS#12 bundle, a .env.
client_secret*.json
service-account*.json
*.p12
.env
.env.*
